            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0527" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2117: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-19T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19, 1919,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your February 16, midnight.</p>
                <p>Department agrees with the suggestion of the Japanese Government that conference
                    of representatives of banking groups be held in New York to arrange details of
                    consortium operation and thinks that negotiations have reached the point where
                    an early meeting is advisable and necessary. In line with that suggestion you
                    may <pb facs="0528" n="426" xml:id="pg426"/> approach the Foreign Office to the
                    end that Japanese Group appoint a representative to attend such a meeting to be
                    held in New York on May 15th. An early expression of agreement to the above will
                    be appreciated in order that plans may be made accordingly.</p>
                <p>Department’s telegram today to Peking will be repeated to you from there.<anchor
                        n="78" xml:id="d360-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
